  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 112 AM MDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nFriday begins the long term with low-level moisture likely \nreplenished along the eastern slopes of the central mountain chain \nfrom the aforementioned cold front. With the monsoon high still \nsquarely over the state, and staying there thru the weekend, this \nwill set the stage for daily rounds of afternoon thunderstorm \nactivity recycling moisture each day with better chances for areas \nalong and immediately east of the central mountain chain relative to \nrecent days. High temperatures also climb back into the upper 90s to \nlow 100s for lower elevation areas, resulting in widespread moderate \nto high heat risk. \n\nThe monsoon high looks to have little movement heading into early \nnext week, favoring a nudge eastward. This will allow for a slight \nuptick in monsoon moisture from the Gulf of CA into the Desert \nSouthwest continuing daily rounds of afternoon thunderstorm \nactivity.",
